WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
On the Home screen, click New project.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The project opens on a blank page: click From template.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
In the Color tab, click Color minimal.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.000
In the Session 1 panel, click Add lights and choose the 436 files of the night.

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Click Open frames: the files of the session open in Inspect.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
On the Darks row, click +, then Add folder… and choose the darks.

7
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Do the same on the Flats row with the flats.

8
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Calibration matching checks the darks and flats against the lights.

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Click Graph to go back to the workflow.

10
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Click the project block and type NGC 2237 in Target: the position is found.

11
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Click Run. The button gives the time the run should take.

12
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Name the project Rosette, pick its folder with Browse…, then click Save.

13
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The run starts: it lists its blocks and the time each should take.

14
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Click Close: the run goes on.

15
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
On the graph, each block shows its progress.

16
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Not shown in real time: the whole run took 34 min 34 s on a graphics card (RTX 4060 Ti).

17
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Each block computed has its bar in green.

18
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Click Post.

19
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Post shows the workflow’s image as one layer. Look before you touch anything.

20
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.000
The empty sky is a milky grey, not a dark one: Sky will correct it.

21
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.000
The outer filaments of the ring barely stand out of the sky: Faint tones will bring them up.

22
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.000
At 100 %, a black line runs along the right edge: Crop will take it off.

23
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.000
At the far left, a dark stain is the shadow of a dust grain: Crop will leave it out.

24
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Drag Sky to the left until the grey veil is gone: here about −1.5.

25
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Drag Faint tones to the right until the outer filaments come up: here about +1.

26
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Click Crop.

27
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Drag the corners of the frame inward: keep the whole ring, leave the edges out.

28
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Click Apply to keep the crop.

29
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Click Export…: TIFF 16-bit is the default format.

30
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Click Export.

31
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.000
The image is written, with its processing history beside it.

32
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Your first image is done. Next tutorial: adjust a block.
